<article class="env-example" id="2964C2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/2964C2">Example <span data-tag="2964C2">7.3.4.4</span>.</a> Filtered colimits are left exact in the $\infty $-category $\SSet $ of spaces; this follows immediately from Proposition <a href="/tag/2A38C8" data-tag="2A38C8">5.3.3.3</a>. It follows that filtered colimits in $\tau _{\leq n} \SSet $ are left exact for each $n \geq -2$, since the full subcategory $\tau _{ \leq n} \SSet \subseteq \SSet $ is stable under filtered colimits and finite limits (in fact, under all limits). </p>
